WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.166 --> 00:00:03.583
Weird West is a game
built on giving the player full control.

00:00:03.583 --> 00:00:06.616
Control the doused enemies in oil before
setting them ablaze.

00:00:06.616 --> 00:00:11.400
Control to bury the dead or dig
em' right backup. To sneak around, go guns

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:15.133
blazing to be a hero, a villain,
or blow the doors off

00:00:15.133 --> 00:00:18.566
instead of finding the key

00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:21.916
It's an immersive sim,
and the core principle of any immersive

00:00:21.916 --> 00:00:25.400
sim is to give the player as much control
as possible

00:00:25.633 --> 00:00:29.666
to allow them to take their own approach,
to craft their own story.

00:00:30.083 --> 00:00:32.833
And of course, the ability to shoot

00:00:32.833 --> 00:00:34.966
absolutely everything

00:00:38.066 --> 00:00:41.083
If you saw a coin on the floor,
you could aim at the coin.

00:00:41.083 --> 00:00:44.716
If you threw a bottle in the air,  jump
and start aiming at the bottle.

00:00:44.933 --> 00:00:48.166
[KURT] That is Raphael Colantino - Raf for short.

00:00:48.466 --> 00:00:52.166
He's the co-director of Dishonored,
director of Prey and founder of Weird West

00:00:52.166 --> 00:00:53.216
Development Studio.

00:00:53.216 --> 00:00:54.983
WolfEye. For Raf,

00:00:54.983 --> 00:00:58.183
Being able to shoot anything in real
time is one of the game's

00:00:58.183 --> 00:01:01.766
most defining mechanics, but it also sent

00:01:01.766 --> 00:01:04.483
the game into development hell.

00:01:04.883 --> 00:01:06.566
There is moments where you really think,

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:09.566
are we screwed?

00:01:11.033 --> 00:01:11.866
When Raf and his team

00:01:11.866 --> 00:01:13.183
set out to make Weird West 

00:01:13.183 --> 00:01:16.633
they wanted to make the actual genre
of weird west (Westerns

00:01:16.633 --> 00:01:20.666
but with horror and fantastical elements)
and put it in an action role

00:01:20.666 --> 00:01:24.566
playing twin stick shooter
set in a fully 3D rendered world.

00:01:26.216 --> 00:01:29.433
After all, all of those things
have existed in one way or another.

00:01:29.450 --> 00:01:32.716
Immersive Sims, isometric RPG, twin
stick shooters -

00:01:32.983 --> 00:01:35.483
All WolfEye needed to do is just combine them.

00:01:37.516 --> 00:01:39.133
What could go wrong?

00:01:40.666 --> 00:01:42.416
A lot, actually.

00:01:42.416 --> 00:01:44.833
We initially had an idea for

00:01:44.966 --> 00:01:48.166
strictly  top-down 2D kind of thing.

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:51.050
All the twin stick shooters
that I had played back then,

00:01:51.233 --> 00:01:55.183
like Nuclear Throne or some other game
where it felt like though

00:01:55.183 --> 00:01:58.566
I had never worked on a twin stick shooter,
it seemed like a sort of problem.

00:01:58.633 --> 00:02:01.366
You aim with one stick
while you move with the other,

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:05.183
and it felt like we could probably do that

00:02:05.183 --> 00:02:08.966
in 3D. It would be a little more pretty.
You're not constrained to a 2D plain

00:02:08.966 --> 00:02:10.316
anymore for combat.

00:02:10.316 --> 00:02:12.133
So we put some elevations. Sooner or later

00:02:12.133 --> 00:02:14.200
you're actually in a free environment.
Like fully 3D.

00:02:14.216 --> 00:02:16.566
Not just for the rendering,
but also for the gameplay.

00:02:16.583 --> 00:02:20.783
But back then what was happening
is that we forgot that we

00:02:20.783 --> 00:02:23.400
our plans for aiming system

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:26.483
was based on, on a 2D system

00:02:26.483 --> 00:02:30.583
and even some, some twin shooters
that are actually rendered in 3D,

00:02:30.583 --> 00:02:32.483
they are still operate on one plain.

00:02:32.483 --> 00:02:36.983
That's the thing that did not click
with us, with any of us.

00:02:37.583 --> 00:02:41.100
Twin stick shooters operate on the core
principle that one analog stick moves

00:02:41.116 --> 00:02:45.416
your character while the other aims
where you shoot and that's it.

00:02:45.716 --> 00:02:49.100
And that control scheme
has remained unchanged since the genre's

00:02:49.100 --> 00:02:52.166
popularization with Robotron back in 1982

00:02:54.433 --> 00:02:55.700
Which is a great game, by the way.

00:02:55.700 --> 00:03:00.500
Now it may have evolved from flat pixels
to fully 3D worlds, but how they operate,

00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:04.616
function and move has remained the same.
You point

00:03:05.383 --> 00:03:07.016
and you shoot

00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:11.366
Weird West, on the other hand,

00:03:11.366 --> 00:03:14.716
well, they wanted to do things
a little different, weirder even.

00:03:15.183 --> 00:03:18.133
As we implemented our
our aiming system

00:03:18.683 --> 00:03:21.916
It was quickly

00:03:22.216 --> 00:03:22.700
hell.

00:03:22.700 --> 00:03:25.316
We quickly realized that we were stuck

00:03:26.233 --> 00:03:28.250
because there was no game
that had pulled that off.

00:03:28.283 --> 00:03:30.283
There was no game
where there were elevations

00:03:30.300 --> 00:03:31.066
and at the same time

00:03:31.066 --> 00:03:34.133
you would aim anywhere
the same way you can in a twin stick shooter.

00:03:34.166 --> 00:03:37.716
The aiming feature we thought
would be planned like four weeks on it,

00:03:37.733 --> 00:03:41.600
but unfortunately it probably took
more like four to six months. 

00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:47.316
[KURT] Even more, the problem arose one year into the 
game's development, putting Raf and his team

00:03:47.316 --> 00:03:49.733
in a pretty tough spot.

00:03:49.733 --> 00:03:53.750
It was out of the question to do,
to not let the player amazing

00:03:53.966 --> 00:03:57.133
and at the same time at this point
was out of the question to go back in 2D.

00:03:57.133 --> 00:04:01.583
And there is moments
where you really think you are we screwed.

00:04:01.766 --> 00:04:06.366
Did we corner ourselves in a way
where that's it?

00:04:06.383 --> 00:04:10.883
We'll never be able to make the game
that we were set to to do.

00:04:11.516 --> 00:04:14.100
The team tried
a lot of different solutions.

00:04:14.116 --> 00:04:17.850
They experimented with a own system where
instead of aiming a thin line of sight,

00:04:17.983 --> 00:04:22.066
the player instead directed a cone
relative to the player's peripheral view.

00:04:22.483 --> 00:04:25.550
However,
it was never a one to one representation

00:04:25.550 --> 00:04:29.116
of the players intention
and what exactly they were aiming at.

00:04:29.333 --> 00:04:31.183
So they scrapped it.

00:04:31.183 --> 00:04:33.883
Then there was the flick system
where the player would cycle

00:04:33.883 --> 00:04:37.166
through targets around them by flicking
the analog stick left and right.

00:04:37.516 --> 00:04:41.600
However, cycling through every object
on screen quickly became tedious

00:04:41.600 --> 00:04:42.800
and cumbersome for the player,

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:47.066
so they limited the player
to only being able to target NPCs,

00:04:48.083 --> 00:04:51.050
which was a No-Go because it
went against the immersive sim philosophy

00:04:51.050 --> 00:04:55.183
of giving the player the freedom
to do what they wanted, how they wanted.

00:04:56.666 --> 00:04:57.950
So they scrapped that too.

00:04:57.950 --> 00:05:00.566
Things weren't not looking good.

00:05:00.683 --> 00:05:05.416
One of the big pillars of the game
was hinging on that thing to be a success.

00:05:05.983 --> 00:05:07.066
It was a lot at stake.

00:05:07.066 --> 00:05:08.616
It would have changed the

00:05:08.616 --> 00:05:12.466
we would have had to change
the nature of the game severely.

00:05:12.466 --> 00:05:13.966
So that was not an option.

00:05:13.966 --> 00:05:17.750
Sometimes you got to make a big shift
and you think "okay, we give up."

00:05:17.783 --> 00:05:19.800
Maybe it would have led to
another type of game,

00:05:19.800 --> 00:05:23.383
like because some time from constraints
emerges something really cool.

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:26.816
But is it pride or a bit of,

00:05:27.233 --> 00:05:29.583
yeah,
I don't know, a bit of ego or something.

00:05:29.900 --> 00:05:31.483
Yeah, we gotta crack that nut.

00:05:31.483 --> 00:05:34.700
They poured months of man hours
into trying to solve

00:05:34.700 --> 00:05:38.100
this problem and were on the verge
of changing the game entirely

00:05:38.266 --> 00:05:41.866
until they had a breakthrough.
[RAF] Nobody believed it was possible.

00:05:41.933 --> 00:05:44.900
Everybody was ready to to give up.

00:05:44.933 --> 00:05:48.866
It took us to two different programmers
to go through that

00:05:48.866 --> 00:05:51.983
and the person
who eventually found the solution

00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:54.266
or at least the beginning of the solution
was...

00:05:54.266 --> 00:05:57.883
Etienne Aubert, our lead
animator, surprisingly.

00:05:57.950 --> 00:05:59.966
And he thought "let's forget the 3D part.

00:05:59.966 --> 00:06:01.700
It's not it's not a 3D thing anymore.

00:06:01.700 --> 00:06:06.350
It's like we render a rectangle
that is constantly facing the camera.

00:06:06.433 --> 00:06:09.916
And even if you move the camera,
the perspective, it will always cut

00:06:09.916 --> 00:06:13.983
what is anything that is under
that line, that's you're moving...

00:06:13.983 --> 00:06:15.433
It's exactly like a cursor.

00:06:15.433 --> 00:06:21.416
It becomes a 2D cursor, even though it's
calculated with 3D stuff."

00:06:23.750 --> 00:06:24.800
[KURT] Instead of trying to

00:06:24.800 --> 00:06:28.633
figure out how to aim in a 3D space
using a 2D control scheme,

00:06:28.650 --> 00:06:32.183
they created an invisible line
tied to the right analog stick.

00:06:32.550 --> 00:06:34.033
Wherever the player pointed it,

00:06:34.033 --> 00:06:37.516
it would render anything in its path
as if it were 2D.

00:06:37.700 --> 00:06:40.783
So regardless of elevation,
whether that's an oil lamp on a table

00:06:40.783 --> 00:06:45.150
or vulgar way up in the sky,
if the line is pointed in its direction,

00:06:45.150 --> 00:06:47.933
it reads as though it is on a flat plain.

00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:53.400
Now that I'm talking about,
it sounds like super obvious,

00:06:53.966 --> 00:06:56.416
but I swear, when when you're stuck in it

00:06:56.416 --> 00:07:01.166
with all the smart people around and like,
most of the time it was like...  "Hmm,

00:07:01.166 --> 00:07:02.350
I don't know."

00:07:02.616 --> 00:07:05.566
You know, so it's funny
that it came from from an artist.

00:07:05.700 --> 00:07:11.966
I think artists, we tend to not be
paralyzed by the knowledge of mass.

00:07:12.383 --> 00:07:17.600
They look at the intention more
than the engineering behind it, you know.

00:07:17.600 --> 00:07:19.733
And so here he had

00:07:20.966 --> 00:07:23.183
he had the great the great solution for us.

00:07:34.133 --> 00:07:35.450
Now, probably one of the most

00:07:35.450 --> 00:07:40.133
amazing parts for me hearing this story
is that if I had not known about it,

00:07:40.333 --> 00:07:44.833
I would have just probably never noticed
anything really remarkable

00:07:45.116 --> 00:07:48.583
about Weird West's aiming system,
which is a good thing.

00:07:48.600 --> 00:07:51.266
That means Raf and the WolfEye Studio team

00:07:51.616 --> 00:07:53.366
did their job

00:07:55.483 --> 00:07:58.850
Even still, despite all the time
they sunk into the game's development

00:07:58.850 --> 00:08:01.633
to be able to execute on the vision
they had intended...

00:08:02.700 --> 00:08:06.933
there's still a 2D mode
you can still just click on overhead mode,

00:08:07.633 --> 00:08:09.950
play the game like that,
and I got to give it to them.

00:08:10.916 --> 00:08:14.966
I think it's pretty fantastic
that they still allow the option despite

00:08:15.616 --> 00:08:18.116
all the work they put in, you know,

00:08:18.116 --> 00:08:20.266
to what they had intended
in the first place.

00:08:20.533 --> 00:08:23.933
In the end, Weird West
is everything it had set out to be.

00:08:24.116 --> 00:08:25.733
It's an isometric RPG,

00:08:25.733 --> 00:08:29.366
it's an immersive sim, and it's a twin
stick shooter all at once.

00:08:29.566 --> 00:08:33.016
Something that was deemed impossible
during the game's development

00:08:33.433 --> 00:08:37.350
that is, if it wasn't
for the perception of an artist.

